#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:25
#: 38fe5e9524654538a38cc5c791e43dee
msgid "Install Atom for Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:27
#: 82a4a83e27d040ce9f727129ccf7c118
msgid "The simplest way to install Atom in your Linux computer, you can go to `https://atom.io <https://atom.io>`__ and downloading the .deb package for Debian/Ubuntu machines, or .rpm package for Red Hat/CentOS/Fedora/SUSE machines. Then run the following command to install it: - Debian and Ubuntu: (deb)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:35
#: 284b37fd29c9423a9ee65ce511d49da2
msgid "Red Hat/CentOS: (yum)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:41
#: caee5ae8f1f042bfba8f4f2ea9e6f755
msgid "Fedora: (dnf)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:47
#: f56b6ea1b0794e3baacbde8f9a8ffa01
msgid "SUSE: (zypp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:54
#: db8e470ccaaf4ff3bd086c7dda7864e9
msgid "Install Atom for Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:56
#: 9bbc20fbb9f34b1c895cab12353ea302
msgid "Installing Atom should be fairly simple. Generally, you can go to `https://atom.io <https://atom.io>`__ and you should see a download button. After finishing download, run the .exe file. This setup program will install Atom, add the atom and apm commands to your PATH, and create shortcuts on the desktop and in the start menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:60
#: 8a505019b833415b9975f6938e306647
msgid "Install Atom for MacOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:62
#: 726063a495f147928ee6ea9738ab59e3
msgid "Atom follows the standard Mac zip installation process. You can either press the download button from the `https://atom.io <https://atom.io>`__ site or you can go to the Atom releases page to download the atom-mac.zip file explicitly. Once you have that file, you can click on it to extract the application and then drag the new Atom application into your \"Applications\" folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:65
#: 58997eeb248641a9bd5a38c784da0ea5
msgid "Configuring GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:67
#: 84794333225b452380ccfa2ccb0d6d4a
msgid "Press on GitHub tab then you should see a prompt like the following. Press on the link to generate a token, then enter this token in the box. Your GitHub account should now be linked with your Atom editor now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:73
#: 7bf4ffa017714fc7908c083cb4135cd4
msgid "You can visit the official GitHub manual for Atom `here <https://flight-manual.atom.io/using-atom/sections/github-package/>`__ to start managing your GitHub repositories from Atom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:76
#: 17aabb24989944d48698542f9bc230b2
msgid "Install Teletype package for real time collaboration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-atom.rst:78
#: b883bb7480db4162a84e81c32e3f6386
msgid "Teletype allows sharing or joining a portal for real time collaboration. To install it, go to the menu bar *Packages->Settings View->Open*. Type in \"Teletype\" in the box then install. Finally, you can see Teletype in the menu *Packages* then you can *\"Join Portal\"* or *\"Share Portal\"*."
msgstr ""

